<Prose
  title="About Us | GoSecurePDF"
  description="Learn about GoSecurePDF and our mission to provide the safest, client-side PDF tools on the internet."
  h1="About GoSecurePDF"
>
  <p>
    GoSecurePDF was born out of a simple, widespread frustration: <strong>Why do we have to compromise our privacy just to edit a PDF document?</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>The Problem with Traditional PDF Tools</h2>
  <p>
    If you search the internet to merge two bank statements, unlock a payroll document, or compress a signed contract, you will find hundreds of free online PDF converters. However, almost all of them require you to <strong>upload your file to their servers</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Once you click "Upload", your most sensitive personal and financial data is stored on a remote server. You have no control over how long they keep it, who has access to it, or whether their servers are secure against hackers. For medical records, legal contracts, and financial documents, this model is a massive security risk.
  </p>

  <h2>The GoSecurePDF Solution</h2>
  <p>
    We built GoSecurePDF with a defining property: <strong>Every single tool runs entirely in your web browser.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    By utilizing cutting-edge <strong>WebAssembly (WASM)</strong> technology, we ported professional-grade PDF processing engines to run directly inside your local browser cache. There is no upload step, no cloud processing server, and no user registration required. 
  </p>
  <p>
    When you compress or merge a PDF on our site, the computational work is done by your own device's CPU. Your files literally never leave your computer.
  </p>

  <h2>Fast, Free, and Private</h2>
  <p>
    Because we don't have to pay for expensive cloud infrastructure to process millions of files, we can afford to offer this suite of powerful tools completely free of charge, with no daily limits or intrusive file-size caps. 
  </p>
  <p>
    Our mission is to provide you with the exact same functionality you expect from premium desktop software, directly on the web, without ever asking you to sacrifice your privacy.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in Touch</h2>
  <p>
    We are constantly working to improve our tools. If you have feature requests, bug reports, or partnership inquiries, please reach out via our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Prose>
